---
---

<section id="about" class="py-20 border-b border-zinc-800">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 lg:gap-8">
    <div class="lg:col-span-4 lg:sticky lg:top-24 h-fit">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-100 mb-4">Il mio approccio<br/>allo sviluppo</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-500 mb-6 font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">[ Le mie basi ingegneristiche ]</p>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        Come futuro ingegnere informatico, l'università mi ha insegnato che il codice è solo il risultato finale di un buon processo di analisi. Nei miei progetti accademici e personali cerco sempre di applicare questi principi:
      </p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="lg:col-span-8">
      <div class="space-y-0">
        <!-- Item 1 -->
        <div class="border-t border-zinc-800 py-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          <div class="md:col-span-1 flex items-center justify-center md:justify-start">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="w-24 h-24 md:w-32 md:h-32 text-emerald-500 opacity-20">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 17.25v1.007a3 3 0 01-.879 2.122L7.5 21h9l-.621-.621A3 3 0 0115 18.257V17.25m6-12V15a2.25 2.25 0 01-2.25 2.25H5.25A2.25 2.25 0 013 15V5.25m18 0A2.25 2.25 0 0018.75 3H5.25A2.25 2.25 0 003 5.25m18 0V12a2.25 2.25 0 01-2.25 2.25H5.25A2.25 2.25 0 013 12V5.25" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="md:col-span-3">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-zinc-200 mb-3">Ingegneria del Software</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
              Capire il problema prima di scrivere il codice. Utilizzo diagrammi UML per schematizzare i casi d'uso e strutturare le idee nei miei progetti universitari e personali.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">UML</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">Use Cases</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">System Specs</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Item 2 -->
        <div class="border-t border-zinc-800 py-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          <div class="md:col-span-1 flex items-center justify-center md:justify-start">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="w-24 h-24 md:w-32 md:h-32 text-emerald-500 opacity-20">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M20.25 6.375c0 2.278-3.694 4.125-8.25 4.125S3.75 8.653 3.75 6.375m16.5 0c0-2.278-3.694-4.125-8.25-4.125S3.75 4.097 3.75 6.375m16.5 0v11.25c0 2.278-3.694 4.125-8.25 4.125s-8.25-1.847-8.25-4.125V6.375m16.5 0v3.75m-16.5-3.75v3.75m16.5 0v3.75C20.25 16.153 16.556 18 12 18s-8.25-1.847-8.25-4.125v-3.75m16.5 0c0 2.278-3.694 4.125-8.25 4.125s-8.25-1.847-8.25-4.125" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="md:col-span-3">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-zinc-200 mb-3">Progettazione Dati</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
              Basi solide nella teoria dei database. So progettare schemi relazionali normalizzati e utilizzare vincoli SQL per mantenere la coerenza dei dati.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">ER Diagrams</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">SQL</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">Normalizzazione</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Item 3 -->
        <div class="border-t border-zinc-800 py-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          <div class="md:col-span-1 flex items-center justify-center md:justify-start">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="w-24 h-24 md:w-32 md:h-32 text-emerald-500 opacity-20">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M17.25 6.75L22.5 12l-5.25 5.25m-10.5 0L1.5 12l5.25-5.25m7.5-3l-4.5 16.5" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="md:col-span-3">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-zinc-200 mb-3">Sviluppo e Architettura</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
              Applicazione pratica dei concetti Object-Oriented. Cerco di scrivere codice pulito seguendo i principi SOLID e architetture base come l'MVC.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">OOP</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">MVC</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">SOLID</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Item 4 -->
        <div class="border-t border-zinc-800 border-b py-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          <div class="md:col-span-1 flex items-center justify-center md:justify-start">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="w-24 h-24 md:w-32 md:h-32 text-emerald-500 opacity-20">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9.813 15.904L9 18.75l-.813-2.846a4.5 4.5 0 00-3.09-3.09L2.25 12l2.846-.813a4.5 4.5 0 003.09-3.09L9 5.25l.813 2.846a4.5 4.5 0 003.09 3.09L15.75 12l-2.846.813a4.5 4.5 0 00-3.09 3.09zM18.259 8.715L18 9.75l-.259-1.035a3.375 3.375 0 00-2.455-2.456L14.25 6l1.036-.259a3.375 3.375 0 002.455-2.456L18 2.25l.259 1.035a3.375 3.375 0 002.456 2.456L21.75 6l-1.035.259a3.375 3.375 0 00-2.456 2.456zM16.894 20.567L16.5 21.75l-.394-1.183a2.25 2.25 0 00-1.423-1.423L13.5 18.75l1.183-.394a2.25 2.25 0 001.423-1.423l.394-1.183.394 1.183a2.25 2.25 0 001.423 1.423l1.183.394-1.183.394a2.25 2.25 0 00-1.423 1.423z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="md:col-span-3">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-zinc-200 mb-3">Esplorazione e AI</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
              Grande curiosità per i nuovi strumenti. Utilizzo regolarmente i Large Language Models (LLM) come supporto allo studio, per velocizzare la scrittura di boilerplate e per imparare nuove tecnologie.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">Prompt Engineering</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-zinc-800/50 text-zinc-400 font-mono text-xs border border-zinc-700/50">AI Coding Assistants</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
